fn-455E6.mechanism:
Saves GBR and sets GBR to 0xFFFF81F8. It reads rpm_current (0xFFFF6624, float) into fr8, the float at 0xFFFF81F8 (GBR+0) into fr9, and the byte at 0xFFFF85D7 into r2.

1) Hysteresis flag at GBR+87 (0xFFFF824F): it is cleared when rpm < [0xD2E9C], set when rpm >= [0xD2EA0], and otherwise left as it was. This is a lower-rpm threshold with hysteresis, assuming [0xD2EA0] > [0xD2E9C].

2) Hysteresis flag at GBR+88 (0xFFFF8250): it is set when rpm >= [0xD2EA8], cleared when rpm < [0xD2EA4], and otherwise held. This is an upper-rpm threshold with hysteresis.

3) Output byte at GBR+62 (0xFFFF8236) is set to 1 if any of the following holds:
- byte 0xFFFF85D7 == 1;
- flag87 == 0;
- flag88 == 1;
- fr9 < [0xD2EAC];
- fr9 >= [0xD2EB0].
Otherwise it compares byte GBR+52 (0xFFFF822C) with the calibration byte at 0xD29A2. The output is 0 if that byte >= the calibration value, else 1.

So the output is 0 only when all four hold: 0xFFFF85D7 != 1, rpm is inside the hysteretic window, the GBR+0 float is inside [C5, C6), and the GBR+52 counter has reached the calibration count. The function then restores the stack and GBR.
